{"name":"Abyssal Waters","hex":"#005765","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"abyssal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belonging to, or resembling, an abyss; unfathomable. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of or belonging to the ocean depths, especially below 2000 metres (6500 ft): abyssal zone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abyssal"},{"term":"waters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of water","Amniotic fluid ."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of water"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waters"}],"entries":[{"title":"Abyssal zone","blocks":[{"text":"The abyssal zone or abyssopelagic zone is a layer of the pelagic zone of the ocean. The word abyss comes from the Greek word ἄβυσσος, meaning \"bottomless\". At depths of 4,000–6,000 m (13,000–20,000 ft), this zone remains in perpetual darkness. It extends across 83% of the total area of the ocean and 60% of Earth's surface. The abyssal zone has temperatures around 2–3 °C (36–37 °F) through the large majority of its mass. The water pressure can reach up to 76 MPa."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abyssal_zone","wikidata":"Q242857"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg/500px-Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg/1280px-Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg/500px-Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dense gathering of Rimicaris hybisae shrimp at the Beebe Hydrothermal Vent Field in the Mid-Cayman Rise. The shrimp are almost entirely blind, surviving at the interface of cold, deep seawater and supercritical hydrothermal fluid.[13]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg"}],"sounds":{"abyssal":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/41/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/41/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav.ogg"}],"waters":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/En-us-waters.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/da/En-us-waters.ogg/En-us-waters.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Cheminée hydrothermale sous une pluie de neige marine (Ifremer 00401-51200)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Chemin%C3%A9e_hydrothermale_sous_une_pluie_de_neige_marine_%28Ifremer_00401-51200%29.jpg/500px-Chemin%C3%A9e_hydrothermale_sous_une_pluie_de_neige_marine_%28Ifremer_00401-51200%29.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chemin%C3%A9e_hydrothermale_sous_une_pluie_de_neige_marine_(Ifremer_00401-51200).jpg","share":0.249375},{"title":"Teal Blue Abstract Magical Fabric Colorful Background 10","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Teal_Blue_Abstract_Magical_Fabric_Colorful_Background_10.jpg/500px-Teal_Blue_Abstract_Magical_Fabric_Colorful_Background_10.jpg","ratio":1.7777777777777777,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teal_Blue_